& [PlanContract] is strict and bounded
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-content-digest/0.1
  + [content_read_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [entry_reference_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  + [expected_content_length] is a u64 and may be zero
  + [maximum_content_bytes] is positive and not greater than 1099511627776
  + [maximum_chunks] is positive and not greater than 1048576
  + [encoded_plan_cap] is exactly 4096 bytes before JSON decode
  = must: expected_content_length is not greater than maximum_content_bytes
  = must: serde JSON denies unknown fields, omissions, wrong types, malformed scalars, and unknown profile
  - never: place supplied chunks, paths, handles, digest assertions, or clocks in the plan

& [AccumulatorContract] is private and validated
  + [construction] occurs only after full plan validation
  + [state] is one Sha256 state, validated plan, observed length zero, and observed chunk count zero
  + [public_inspection] is immutable plan and counter getters only
  + [state_size] is independent of total content length
  - never: expose mutable hash state, retain chunks, implement serialization, or offer an unchecked constructor

& [ChunkTransitionContract] is consuming and atomic
  + [input] is one borrowed nonempty caller-supplied byte slice
  + [signature] consumes accumulator and returns Result of next accumulator or one fault
  + [chunk_length] converts exactly to u64 or faults resource
  + [next_chunk_count] uses checked addition and does not exceed maximum_chunks
  + [next_observed_length] uses checked addition and does not exceed expected_content_length or maximum_content_bytes
  + [mutation_order] validates all next values before hashing exact input bytes
  + [hash_input] is accepted chunks in call order with no framing, delimiter, normalization, text decoding, skip, reorder, or duplication
  + [fault] returns no accumulator or observation

& [EmptyContentContract] is exact
  + expected length zero admits zero chunks only
  + consuming finalization from the initial state derives e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
  + any empty chunk is rejected as chunk
  + any nonempty chunk under zero expected length is rejected as length

& [FinalizationContract] is consuming and exact
  + consume the accumulator exactly once
  + require observed length equals expected content length
  + finalize SHA-256 and encode lowercase 64-character hexadecimal
  + return one supplied-content observation with every plan field, observed length, observed chunk count, and digest
  - never: return success for short, excessive, or rejected content

& [ObservationContract] is output only
  + [fields] are profile, content-read identity, entry-reference identity, expected length, observed length, maximum-content bytes, maximum chunks, observed chunks, and digest
  + [inspection] is immutable getters and serde Serialize
  + [construction] is private to successful finalization
  - never: expose fields publicly, derive Deserialize, implement Default, or provide a public constructor

& [StabilityBindingContract] reuses current authority
  + [input_1] is one successful supplied-content observation
  + [input_2] is one WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityInput
  + [validation] calls reconcile_windows_supplied_entry_stability on input_2
  + [nested_failure] preserves exact WindowsSuppliedEntryStabilityFault under code stability
  + [kind] requires regular_file
  + [entry_reference] requires exact equality between observation and stable-pair common entry reference
  + [metadata_length] requires pre-read and post-read end_of_file both equal expected and observed content lengths
  + [output] preserves complete observation and complete stable pair
  - never: accept WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair as direct input
  - never: accept directory kind, tolerate a length delta, or collapse the stable pair

& [BindingOutputContract] is output only
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-content-digest/0.1
  + [content_observation] is complete
  + [stable_pair] is complete
  + [inspection] is immutable getters and serde Serialize
  - never: derive Deserialize, provide public fields, or provide a public constructor

& [FaultContract] is closed and bounded
  + [codes] are json, profile, content_read_identity, entry_reference_identity, limit, chunk, length, stability, kind, entry_reference, metadata_length, and resource
  + [nested_stability_fault] is present exactly for stability and absent otherwise
  + [field] is deterministic and no longer than 64 Unicode scalar values
  + [message] is deterministic and no longer than 256 Unicode scalar values
  + [release] is exactly one fault with no partial success or resumable failed accumulator
  - never: include supplied bytes, hash state, or unbounded encoded input in diagnostics

& [SemanticStrengthContract] prevents provenance inflation
  + [supplied_chunk] means bytes presented by the caller
  + [derived_digest] means SHA-256 of exact accepted chunk concatenation
  + [content_observation] means derived evidence about supplied bytes only
  + [stable_binding] means structural syntax and length agreement with a newly reconciled supplied stable pair
  + [identities] remain caller-owned local syntax
  - never: claim bytes came from a file, handle, path, filesystem, platform, one read, or the stable metadata subject
  - never: claim physical order, freshness, query completion, initialized buffers, completeness, content stability, supported platform, trust, authenticity, atomic snapshot, or immutability

& [DataDesignContract] is explicit
  + [conceptual_model] derive exact supplied-byte digest then join it to revalidated supplied stable metadata under closed gates
  + [logical_model] strict plan to accumulator transitions to observation, then stability reconciliation to binding
  + [physical_model] safe deterministic in-memory Rust using serde and sha2
  + [identity_namespace] caller-owned and invocation local
  + [source_data] plan, borrowed chunks, and stability input
  + [derived_state] private accumulator
  + [derived_projection] content observation or stable binding
  + [persistence] absent

& [ImplementationBoundary] is zero effect
  + [authorized_file] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_content_digest.rs
  + [authorized_export] is one exact library-module export
  + [authorized_tests] are module unit tests, one independent static test, one evidence rehash test, and workspace regression tests
  + [plan_json_byte_cap] is 4096
  + [message_scalar_cap] is 256
  + [field_scalar_cap] is 64
  + [Cargo_delta] is zero because sha2 is already a direct dependency
  + [lockfile_delta] is zero
  + [unsafe] is denied
  + [production_imports] are std, serde, sha2, and windows_supplied_entry_stability
  - never: use windows-sys, filesystem, process, environment, clock, random, network, model, persistence, handle, pointer, physical query, path, traversal, Git, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion APIs

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-SCD-001 through M2B-SCD-014
  + [requirements] are strict plan, private state, consuming transition, checked accounting, exact SHA-256, empty behavior, exact finalization, output-only observation, stability revalidation, exact join gates, preservation, bounded faults, semantic nonclaims, and proof closure

& [AcceptanceContract] is exact
  + [source] manifest matches exact SHA-256 and byte count
  + [authority] governing signature binds every processed SJS stage and current stability signature
  + [focused] unit and independent static tests pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [vectors] empty, abc, multi-chunk, and partition-equivalent exact digests pass
  + [behavior] every requirement, limit, transition fault, finalize gate, binding gate, and output preservation rule has a direct test or static proof edge
  + [effects] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, platform, and runtime-effect deltas remain zero
  + [evidence] clone-portable manifest hashes canonical, module, tests, solution, proof, review, and narrative
  + [global] workspace debug and release tests, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and audit pass
  + [downstream_gate] physical producer, path and Git projection, directory and root stability, traversal, receipt, and admission remain absent

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure implementation only
  + [allowed] one deterministic module, export, serialization, focused tests, static test, evidence support, solution, proof, review, and governed narrative
  + [forbidden] physical I/O or origin claims, Win32, windows-sys, unsafe, handles, pointers, filesystems, process, environment, clocks, networks, persistence, models, paths, traversal, Git, receipts, admission, mutation, sealing, cleanup, or promotion

